id rgb(203, 213, 225); background: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(15, 23, 42); min-width: 150px; cursor: pointer; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; width: 100%;"><span style="overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;">All</span><span style="font-size: 0.8em; margin-left: 8px;">▼</span></div></div><div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1rem;"><button style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; background: rgb(37, 99, 235); color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: medium; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.85rem; width: 100%;">Select All</button><button style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; background: rgb(220, 38, 38); color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: medium; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.85rem; width: 100%;">Clear Selection</button><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox" checked=""><span>Show theoretical heat pumps (1)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Carnot and the best technology archetype, as reference points against the modelled machines.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot source-limited points (7)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover only part of the demand above T_sink, so they lie off the sink profile.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot demand-limited points (23)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover the full demand but leave waste heat unused at T_source, so they lie off the source profile.</span></span></label><p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); text-align: center; font-weight: 500;">Feasible Combinations: 289<br><span style="font-weight: 400;">shown in chart: 259</span></p></div><div><label style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500;">COP MODEL</label><select style="padding: 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid rgb(203, 213, 225); background: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(15, 23, 42); min-width: 150px;" title="2 temps: source return and sink supply. 4 temps: also source supply and sink return, both taken from the pinch (pinch − ΔTmin/2 and pinch + ΔTmin/2)."><option value="2t">Model 2 temps</option><option value="4t">Model 4 temps</option></select></div><div class="cf-trigger-block"><div class="cf-trigger-head"><label style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500;">COP SOURCE</label><div class="chart-help-container inline"><button class="btn btn-sm chart-help-btn  " title="Show explanation"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-info" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4"></path><path d="M12 8h.01"></path></svg></button></div></div><button class="cf-trigger ">ƒ Use my own COP formula<span class="cf-trigger-sub">Paste a custom COP to perform integration and optimization with your own heat pump.</span></button></div></div><div class="pa-opt-chart" style="display: flex; min-width: 0px; overflow: hidden;"><div data-testid="chart">{"points":"259:e66aa9f0","maxQ":"Test@113","selected":[],"pinch":73,"mode":"net_load"}<button data-testid="chart-pick"></button></div></div></div></div></div></div>"`;

